            format: HTML
            text: |
              <p><span class="Qnum">[K] </span><span class="Qtxt">¿Golpearla, es decir, golpearla una y otra vez tan fuerte como sea posible?</span></p>
  - name: MICS7FS.FCD4
    conditions:
      - questionText:
          EN:
            format: HTML
            text: |
              <p><span class="Inum">FCD4. </span><span class="Itxt">Check FS4: Has this respondent already responded to the following question (UCD5) for another child?</span></p>
          ES:
            format: HTML
            text: |
              <p><span class="Inum">FCD4. </span><span class="Itxt">Marque FS4: ¿Este encuestado ya respondió a la siguiente pregunta (UCD5) para otro niño?</span></p>
  - name: MICS7FS.FCD5
    conditions:
      - questionText:
          EN:
            format: HTML
            text: |
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCD5. </span><span class="Qtxt">Do you believe that in order to bring up, raise, or educate a child properly, the child needs to be physically punished?</span></p>
          ES:
            format: HTML
            text: |
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCD5. </span><span class="Qtxt">¿Cree que para criar, criar o educar adecuadamente a un niño, es necesario castigarlo físicamente?</span></p>
  - name: MICS7FS.FCF1
    conditions:
      - questionText:
          EN:
            format: HTML
            text: |
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCF1. </span><span class="Qtxt">I would like to ask you some questions about difficulties <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> may have.</span></p>
              <p><span class="Qtxt">Does <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> wear glasses <span class="QtxtC">or contact lenses</span>?</span></p>
          ES:
            format: HTML
            text: |
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCF1. </span><span class="Qtxt">Me gustaría hacerle algunas preguntas sobre las dificultades que puede tener <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span>.</span></p>
              <p><span class="Qtxt">¿<span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> usa anteojos <span class="QtxtC">o lentes de contacto</span>?</span></p>
  - name: MICS7FS.FCF2
    conditions:
      - questionText:
          EN:
            format: HTML
            text: |
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCF2. </span><span class="Qtxt">Does <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> use a hearing aid?</span></p>
          ES:
            format: HTML
            text: |
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCF2. </span><span class="Qtxt">¿<span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> utiliza un audífono?</span></p>
  - name: MICS7FS.FCF3
    conditions:
      - questionText:
          EN:
            format: HTML
            text: |
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCF3. </span><span class="Qtxt">Does <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> use any equipment or receive assistance for walking?</span></p>
          ES:
            format: HTML
            text: |
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCF3. </span><span class="Qtxt">¿<span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> utiliza algún equipo o recibe ayuda para caminar?</span></p>
  - name: MICS7FS.FCF6
    conditions:
      - logic: FCF1<>1 and chsex=1
        questionText:
          EN:
            format: HTML
            text: |
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCF4. </span><span class="Qtxt">In the following questions, I will ask you to answer by selecting one of four possible answers. For each question, would you say that <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> has: 1) no difficulty, 2) some difficulty, 3) a lot of difficulty, or 4) that he cannot at all.</span></p>
              <p><span class="Itxt">Repeat the categories during the individual questions whenever the respondent does not use an answer category: </span><span class="Qtxt">Remember the four possible answers: Would you say that <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> has: 1) no difficulty, 2) some difficulty, 3) a lot of difficulty, or 4) that he cannot at all?</span></p>
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCF6B. </span><span class="Qtxt">Does <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> have difficulty seeing?</span></p>
          ES:
            format: HTML
            text: |
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCF4. </span><span class="Qtxt">En las siguientes preguntas, le pediré que responda seleccionando una de cuatro respuestas posibles. Para cada pregunta, ¿diría que <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> tiene: 1) ninguna dificultad, 2) alguna dificultad, 3) mucha dificultad, o 4) que no puede en absoluto.</span></p>
              <p><span class="Itxt">Repita las categorías durante las preguntas individuales siempre que el encuestado no utilice una categoría de respuesta: </span><span class="Qtxt">Recuerde las cuatro posibles respuestas: ¿Diría que <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> tiene: 1) ninguna dificultad, 2) alguna dificultad, 3) mucha dificultad, o 4) que no puede en absoluto?</span></p>
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCF6B. </span><span class="Qtxt">¿Tiene <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> dificultades para ver?</span></p>
      - logic: FCF1=1 and chsex=1
        questionText:
          EN:
            format: HTML
            text: |
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCF4. </span><span class="Qtxt">In the following questions, I will ask you to answer by selecting one of four possible answers. For each question, would you say that <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> has: 1) no difficulty, 2) some difficulty, 3) a lot of difficulty, or 4) that he cannot at all.</span></p>
              <p><span class="Itxt">Repeat the categories during the individual questions whenever the respondent does not use an answer category: </span><span class="Qtxt">Remember the four possible answers: Would you say that <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> has: 1) no difficulty, 2) some difficulty, 3) a lot of difficulty, or 4) that he cannot at all?</span></p>
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCF6A. </span><span class="Qtxt">When wearing his glasses <span class="QtxtC">or contact lenses</span>, does <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> have difficulty seeing?</span></p>
          ES:
            format: HTML
            text: |
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCF4. </span><span class="Qtxt">En las siguientes preguntas, le pediré que responda seleccionando una de cuatro respuestas posibles. Para cada pregunta, ¿diría que <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> tiene: 1) ninguna dificultad, 2) alguna dificultad, 3) mucha dificultad, o 4) que no puede en absoluto.</span></p>
              <p><span class="Itxt">Repita las categorías durante las preguntas individuales siempre que el encuestado no utilice una categoría de respuesta: </span><span class="Qtxt">Recuerde las cuatro posibles respuestas: ¿Diría que <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> tiene: 1) ninguna dificultad, 2) alguna dificultad, 3) mucha dificultad, o 4) que no puede en absoluto?</span></p>
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCF6A. </span><span class="Qtxt">Cuando usa sus gafas <span class="QtxtC">o lentes de contacto</span>, ¿<span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> tiene dificultades para ver?</span></p>
      - logic: FCF1<>1 and chsex=2
        questionText:
          EN:
            format: HTML
            text: |
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCF4. </span><span class="Qtxt">In the following questions, I will ask you to answer by selecting one of four possible answers. For each question, would you say that <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> has: 1) no difficulty, 2) some difficulty, 3) a lot of difficulty, or 4) that she cannot at all.</span></p><p><span class="Itxt">Repeat the categories during the individual questions whenever the respondent does not use an answer category: </span><span class="Qtxt">Remember the four possible answers: Would you say that <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> has: 1) no difficulty, 2) some difficulty, 3) a lot of difficulty, or 4) that she cannot at all?</span></p><p><span class="Qnum">FCF6B. </span><span class="Qtxt">Does <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> have difficulty seeing?</span></p><p></p>
          ES:
            format: HTML
            text: |
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCF4.</span><span class="Qtxt">En las siguientes preguntas, le pediré que responda seleccionando una de cuatro respuestas posibles. Para cada pregunta, ¿diría que <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span>&nbsp;tiene: 1) ninguna dificultad, 2) alguna dificultad, 3) mucha dificultad, o 4) que no puede en absoluto.</span></p><p><span class="Itxt">Repita las categorías durante las preguntas individuales siempre que el encuestado no utilice una categoría de respuesta:&nbsp;</span><span class="Qtxt">Recuerde las cuatro posibles respuestas: ¿Diría que <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span>&nbsp;tiene: 1) ninguna dificultad, 2) alguna dificultad, 3) mucha dificultad o 4) que no puede en absoluto?</span></p><p><span class="Qnum">FCF6B.</span><span class="Qtxt">¿Tiene <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span>&nbsp;dificultad para ver?</span></p><p></p>
      - logic: FCF1=1 and chsex=2
        questionText:
          EN:
            format: HTML
            text: |
              <p><span class="Qnum">FCF4. </span><span class="Qtxt">In the following questions, I will ask you to answer by selecting one of four possible answers. For each question, would you say that <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> has: 1) no difficulty, 2) some difficulty, 3) a lot of difficulty, or 4) that she cannot at all.</span></p><p><span class="Itxt">Repeat the categories during the individual questions whenever the respondent does not use an answer category: </span><span class="Qtxt">Remember the four possible answers: Would you say that <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> has: 1) no difficulty, 2) some difficulty, 3) a lot of difficulty, or 4) that she cannot at all?</span></p><p><span class="Qnum">FCF6A. </span><span class="Qtxt">When wearing her glasses <span class="QtxtC">or contact lenses</span>, does <span class="REF">~~FS3A~~</span> have difficulty seeing?</span></p><p></p>
          ES:
